  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): ブッソウゲ",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%96%E3%83%83%E3%82%BD%E3%82%A6%E3%82%B2",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 110519783,
      "text": "ブッソウゲ は、アオイ科フヨウ属の低木。扶桑花、仏桑華とも。沖縄では赤花ともいう。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Hibiscus × rosa-sinensis",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus_%C3%97_rosa-sinensis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1378428895,
      "text": "Hibiscus × rosa-sinensis is a cultigen of tropical hibiscus, a flowering plant in the Hibiscus genus and Hibisceae tribe of the family Malvaceae."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Hibiscus rosa-sinensis",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus_rosa-sinensis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 171581888,
      "text": "Hibiscus rosa-sinensis, llamado comúnmente rosa de China, cayena,  amapola, hibisco, gumamela, entre otros nombres, es un arbusto perennifolio de la familia de las malváceas, originario de Asia oriental."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Hibiscus Rose de Chine",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus_Rose_de_Chine",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 239947007,
      "text": "L'Hibiscus Rose de Chine ou Ketmie est une espèce d’arbuste ornemental tropical de la famille des Malvaceae."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Hibiscus rosa-sinensis",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus_rosa-sinensis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 71312788,
      "text": "O mimo-de-vênus, também conhecido por hibisco, papoula ou graxa-de-estudante, é um arbusto lenhoso, fibroso, com até 5 metros de altura, originário da Ásia tropical e do Havaí, onde é considerado a flor nacional. Possui 5 000 variedades. Muito difundido no mundo pelas propriedades ornamentais, possui diversas variedades e formas, com flores grandes ou pequenas, geralmente vermelhas, com pétalas lisas ou crespas. As folhas, variegadas ou não, podem ser largas ou estreitas. Muito cultivado no Brasil, com vários híbridos e variedades, é utilizado com muito sucesso na arborização urbana abaixo da rede elétrica, devido ao pequeno porte, necessitando condução e poda, além de enfeitar jardins, praças e servir de cerca-viva."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Kembang sepatu",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kembang_sepatu",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 28935325,
      "text": "Kembang sepatu, bunga sepatu, bunga raya, wara-wiri atau worawiri adalah tumbuhan semak dari famili Malvaceae yang berasal dari wilayah Asia Timur dan banyak ditanam sebagai tanaman hias di daerah tropis dan subtropis. Bunganya besar, berwarna merah, putih, atau kuning muda dan tidak berbau. Bunga dari berbagai kultivar dan kacukan ini bisa berupa bunga tunggal atau bunga ganda yang berwarna putih hingga kuning, jingga hingga merah tua atau merah jambu."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Hibiscus × rosa-sinensis § Cultivation",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus_%C3%97_rosa-sinensis#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 1378428895,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "Hibiscus × rosa-sinensis is widely grown as an ornamental plant throughout the tropics and subtropics. As it does not tolerate temperatures below 10 °C (50 °F), in temperate regions it is best grown under glass. Plants grown in containers may be placed outside during the summer months and moved into shelter during the winter months.\nNumerous cultivars exist, with flower colors ranging from white through yellow and orange to scarlet and shades of pink, with both single and double sets of petals. The cultivar 'Cooperi' has gained the Royal Horticultural Society's Award of Garden Merit.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
